# Installation

Get {{ projectName }} up and running in your project.

## Prerequisites

Before installing {{ projectName }}, ensure you have:

- Node.js 18 or later
- A package manager (bun, npm, yarn, or pnpm)

## Install {{ projectName }}

Choose your preferred package manager:

```bash title="Using bun (recommended)"
bun add {{ projectName }}
```

```bash title="Using npm"
npm install {{ projectName }}
```

```bash title="Using yarn"
yarn add {{ projectName }}
```

```bash title="Using pnpm"
pnpm add {{ projectName }}
```

## Verify Installation

You can verify the installation by importing {{ projectName }} in your project:

```typescript
import {{ "{" }} main {{ "}" }} from '{{ projectName }}';

console.log('{{ projectName }} is installed!');
```

## Development Installation

If you want to contribute to {{ projectName }} or run it locally:

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone {% if githubRepo %}{{ githubRepo }}{% else %}https://github.com/your-org/{{ projectName }}{% endif %}
cd {{ projectName }}

# Install dependencies
bun install

# Run tests
bun test

# Build the project
bun run build
```

## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

**Installation fails with permission errors**
Try using a different package manager or check your Node.js installation.

**Module not found errors**
Ensure you're using the correct import path and that the package is properly installed.

## Next Steps

Now that you have {{ projectName }} installed, check out the [Quick Start guide](/quick-start/) to begin using it.